<p>Given that I typically take a wait-and-see attitude when Apple introduces a new product, I was surprised to find myself ordering a <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-homeview/">HomeView</a> within a day of its announcement. I was even more surprised when lots of otherwise pro-Apple people—<a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/10/homeview_thoughts_and_observations">this guy</a>, for example—were skeptical about its value.</p>
<p><img alt="HomeView" class="ss" src="https://leancrew.com/all-this/images2026/20261020-HomeView.png" title="HomeView" width="80%"/></p>
<p>Why is this? Well, one reason could be that I don’t already have a HomePod in my kitchen, which makes me behind the times. I’ve been thinking I should get one (or two), but Siri’s deficiencies have kept me back. Also, I like the idea of a status board but didn’t want to dedicate an iPad to that. The recently improved Siri and the HomeView’s touchscreen kill those two birds with one $300 stone.</p>
<p>And I think I have a good place for it in my kitchen. Not on the center island. The two likely spots for it on the island are corners that are already taken:</p>
<ul>
<li>The corner that currently has a shallow wooden bowl that my dad turned and that I finished after his death. It’s where I put fruit and vegetables that don’t need refrigeration and is currently holding an avocado that should be ripe tomorrow.</li>
<li>The corner that has a vase I keep filled with flowers from Trader Joe’s. That’s where Janet put flowers, and it isn’t going to change.</li>
</ul>
<p>Another obvious place would be the kitchen desk. Many years ago, we had a laptop computer on the desk, so it has a history of similar use. But the desk isn’t in a great spot for the HomeView—a little too far away from the island to look at it while I’m preparing a meal, and maybe a little too far away from the kitchen table to use as a status board.</p>
<p>But there is a perfect spot at the end of one of the counters. It’s near both the kitchen table and the island. I’ll need to rotate it, depending on where I am, but <a href="https://www.apple.com/105/media/us/apple-homeview/2026/f7ce47a8-10f2-455c-b99f-bf9b85a35cb6/films/product/apple-homeview-product-tpl-us-2026_16x9.m3u8">the annoying family in the video</a> showed that that was no problem. And there’s an outlet right there, so the power cord can be stored neatly.</p>
<p>The counter isn’t a good spot for a FaceTime call, but it’ll be easy to move the HomeView over to the kitchen table when I use it for that.</p>
<p>So by being behind the times for several years, I’m now in the perfect position to be on the cutting edge. With a product <a href="https://gizmodo.com/apples-homeviews-reportedly-collected-dust-in-warehouses-for-the-better-part-of-a-year-2000827427">that’s been sitting on the shelf</a> for a year or so.</p>
